            "notes": "## Round 3 ##\n---\n### \u26a1 Powers: ###\n- [Medicinal Missiles](item_30eeab6c-4a1e-4a16-b9dd-e83d633caa40) gives huge *impact* at this point\n- [Cosmic Coolant](item_5584169d-94af-4efa-955c-263353a75553) can be great if you plan to go more aggressive and build into the blaster later, but the addition of [Biotech Maximizer](item_01c6dcb3-d2e2-4c57-bd21-61d7b8f939c4) this round should make [Medicinal Missiles](item_30eeab6c-4a1e-4a16-b9dd-e83d633caa40) the default\n---\n### \ud83d\udca3 Items: ###\n- [Biotech Maximizer](item_01c6dcb3-d2e2-4c57-bd21-61d7b8f939c4) and [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56) keeps missles shooting more often and more effectively\n- [Lock-On Shield](item_220287f8-1dc5-4a6c-9e86-c14cf970b689) continues to give freedom to use the torpedoes where you want\n---\n### \u2699\ufe0f Optional: ###\n- [Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643) early can really help with survivability while also keeping your build a little more well-rounded if you feel ok with the cooldown rate of torpedoes\n- Depending on how the previous rounds went, pick from any of the **Optional** items; whether you have extra money and are adding something, or are swapping some out due to your current needs and cash flow, get what you need\n---\n### \ud83c\udfae Playstyle: ###\n- Don't sit on torpedoes, you should be able to keep them flying out often to keep maximum *impact*",
