            "notes": "## Round 7 ##\n---\n### \u26a1 Powers: ###\n- If you're buffing the ring, [Black Hole](item_d9edbd0b-d1e2-4103-b8d4-6e1dc8124894) will really swing a teamfight with this right in the middle of it\n- You can definitely also go the [Stinger](item_e9d0d530-d620-4e74-a34d-38cdebfeb9a4) route and grab a [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) and/or [Liquid Nitrogen](item_a8d99526-05a3-4405-babb-b025479b1b98) instead for a similar effect depending on your playstyle\n---\n### \ud83d\udca3 Items: ###\n- Even if all-in with your ring at this point, having [Three-tap Tommygun](item_39c5d2a4-1db0-444f-86d9-2a1e9a331429) (remember the 3% only works on enemy damage not healing) can be great to keep both torpedo output high, and your blaster will hopefully be able to keep up with the craziness of a Round 7, especially with an [Amari's Antidote](item_67e0b1c5-3bcb-4ab5-b818-5082e5706124) to help round out the blaster\n-If you are **all-in** on the blaster, drop [Biotech Maximizer](item_01c6dcb3-d2e2-4c57-bd21-61d7b8f939c4) and [Iridescent Iris](item_b7fb28ef-ce82-416b-8693-01c274f8df4e) and grab [Liquid Nitrogen](item_a8d99526-05a3-4405-babb-b025479b1b98) with [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) and get aggressive\n---\n### \u2699\ufe0f Optional: ###\n- Pick from any of the **Optional** items; whether you have extra money and are adding something, or are swapping some out due to your current needs and cash flow\n---\n### \ud83c\udfae Playstyle: ###\n- Regardless of if you went for the ring, or the blaster output, keep your *impact* high with constant cooldown spam and aggression and take your Round 7, you got this!",
